> Time: 1431354990 / Mon, 11 May 2015 14:36:30 +0000
> URL: /index.php?/REST/Forums/topic/getPosts?topicId=71738&start=80&SessionId=41a5f7089aa2fb84640b0f9136c1ba6d
> User Jaycee31 (282805)
Request Time: 1 seconds
{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":71738,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"157661478545570618cfaf38c32e8a9b","RawContent":"[quote name=\"Mel K\"]\nHi Ladies! Congrats to all the future 2014 brides, so exciting...and stressful, who knew! lol I&#039;m freaking out a little bit, we are getting married april 20, 2014, as of now we have 75 booked, insane! We had origionally booked the private restaurant ( we were only expecting 40-50 to book) but im second guessing it now with a minimum cost of $45\/pp with such a large number. Basically from what i&#039;ve read, the only options are ; 1. private dinner ($) 2. a la carte for 30 guests at most (free) 3. buffet so am I correct in assuming with this many guests and without paying a per head price my only option is buffet?? Does anyone know if its possible to pay to rent out an a la carte? I&#039;ve read posts that said yes but that was in 2008\/2011 posts. Thanks so much, I&#039;m also having a hard time getting a response and I do understand the weddings are still a year away but a woman needs to plan!! lol[\/quote] [b]Wow! That&#039;s a large group...it will be pricey at $20 per person after the included 8 plus $45 per person for the private reception. You could do the buffet (included) or rather than the private reception, you could do a cocktail reception at $15 per person. I haven&#039;t seen anything about renting an a-la-carte. I can&#039;t see them doing that because that would mean closing it to the rest of the resort guests. I don&#039;t know yet how many we will have actually book, but I sure wish I did!! I understand the wanting to have a plan to confirm what you will actually choose to do! Good luck and keep me posted![\/b]","Attachments":[],"Id":1746797,"PostDate":1365989026,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <blockquote class='ipsBlockquote' data-author=\"Mel K\" url=\"\/t\/84026\/any&#045;2014&#045;grand&#045;palladium&#045;jamaica&#045;brides&#045;about&#045;yet\/60#post_1892984\"><p>Hi Ladies! Congrats to all the future 2014 brides, so exciting...and stressful, who knew! lol I'm freaking out a little bit, we are getting married april 20, 2014, as of now we have 75 booked, insane! We had origionally booked the private restaurant ( we were only expecting 40-50 to book)\u00a0but im second guessing it now with a minimum cost of $45\/pp with such a large number. Basically from what i've read, the only options are ; 1. private dinner ($) 2. a la carte for 30 guests at most (free) 3. buffet so am I correct in assuming with this many guests and without paying a per head price my only option is buffet?? Does anyone know if its possible to pay to rent out an a la carte? I've read posts that said yes but that was in 2008\/2011 posts. Thanks so much, I'm also having a hard time getting a response and I do understand the weddings are still a year away but a woman needs to plan!! lol<\/p><\/blockquote> <strong class='bbc'>Wow! That's a large group...it will be pricey at $20 per person after the included 8 plus $45 per person for the private reception. You could do the buffet (included) or rather than the private reception, you could do a cocktail reception at $15 per person. I haven't seen anything about renting an a-la-carte. I can't see them doing that because that would mean closing it to the rest of the resort guests. I don't know yet how many we will have actually book, but I sure wish I did!! I understand the wanting to have a plan to confirm what you will actually choose to do! Good luck and keep me posted!<\/strong>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"cindyleaman@hotmail.om","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1362098921,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-266722.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"CindyLou","Id":266722,"Name":"CindyLou","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":71738,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7e289da5c766f8c00b7ca6b3afe79c31","RawContent":"Hey everyone! I am going to talk to my travel agent tomorrow about switching to GPJ, it looks amazing, Our wedding is booked for march 3rd, 2014 at the Riu MoBay, we stayed at the riu this year and absolutely loved it! However we just got our group rates back for this trip which are hardly \"group rates\" at all, not even close to what we expected or what we expect our guests to pay! I&#039;m hoping our travel agent will have more luck contacting the coordinators, I hear they are busy and hard to get ahold of... I am slightly freaking out that nothing will be available!! :( Fingers crossed I will be posting again in this group!","Attachments":[],"Id":1746831,"PostDate":1366000186,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n              